---
const noFeatures = ['Transaction feeds', 'Spending categories', 'Envelopes', 'Bank sync'];
---

<section>
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal="up">
      Non-feature
    </p>
    <h2 data-reveal="up" style="--reveal-delay: 0.08s">
      Not a <span class="accent">budgeting app</span>
    </h2>
    <ul class="chips" data-reveal>
      <li class="yes">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M3.5 8.5l3 3 6-7"></path>
        </svg>
        Net worth over years
      </li>
      {noFeatures.map((item, i) => (
        <li class="no" style={`--i: ${i}`}>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M4.5 4.5l7 7m0-7l-7 7"></path>
          </svg>
          <span class="sr-only">Not included: </span>
          <s>{item}</s>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p>
      Leaving those out is deliberate: they’re non-features, not missing features. Budgeting apps
      answer <em>“where did my coffee money go?”</em> Balances answers a different question:{' '}
      <em>“is my household building wealth over time?”</em>
    </p>
    <p>
      If you love itemising every purchase, keep your budgeting app. Balances sits above it,
      tracking the number that actually moves: your net worth.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  section {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .container {
    padding-block: var(--section-pad-top) 4rem;
    max-width: 60rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  p {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
  }

  em {
    color: var(--secondary-foreground);
  }

  .chips {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0.5rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .chips li {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.375rem 0.875rem 0.375rem 0.4375rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .chips svg {
    width: 1.375rem;
    height: 1.375rem;
    padding: 0.25rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    fill: none;
    stroke: currentColor;
    stroke-width: 2;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }

  .yes {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    background: color-mix(in oklch, var(--primary) 14%, transparent);
    color: var(--secondary-foreground);
  }

  .yes svg {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary-foreground);
  }

  .no {
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
  }

  .no svg {
    background: var(--muted);
  }

  /* The strike is drawn as a line (not text-decoration) so it can animate
     across; <s> keeps the meaning for assistive tech. */
  .no s {
    position: relative;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .no s::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset-inline: -0.125rem;
    top: 55%;
    border-top: 1px solid currentColor;
  }

  /* Phones: one item per line, left-aligned under each other like a
     checklist, with the pill chrome dropped. */
  @media (max-width: 36rem) {
    .chips {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 0.625rem;
      width: fit-content;
      margin-inline: auto;
    }

    .chips li {
      padding: 0;
      border: 0;
      background: none;
      font-size: 0.9375rem;
    }
  }

  /* Motion (paused until in view; see global.css): the tick pops, then a line
     strikes through each budgeting feature in turn. */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .yes svg {
      animation: pop 0.5s cubic-bezier(0.3, 1.6, 0.5, 1) 0.2s both;
    }

    .no s::after {
      transform-origin: left;
      animation: strike 0.45s ease-in-out both;
      animation-delay: calc(0.55s + var(--i) * 0.22s);
    }
  }

  @keyframes pop {
    from {
      scale: 0;
    }
  }

  @keyframes strike {
    from {
      scale: 0 1;
    }
  }
</style>
